---
title: Cold Peanut Ginger Noodles
author: Melissa Clark
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/780934238-cold-peanut-ginger-noodles
tags: noodles, peanut butter, ginger, vegetarian, vegan, make-ahead, quick, weeknight, summer
cook time: 15 minutes
servings: 6
date added: 2026-09-01
---

Bring a #large pot{} of salted water to a boil. Add the @Chinese egg noodles, spaghetti or linguine{16%oz} and cook according to package instructions. Drain, reserving about ⅔ cup of starchy pasta water.

While the pasta cooks, in a #large bowl{}, combine @crunchy peanut butter{1%cup}, @soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @chile crisp{2%tbsp}, @sesame oil{2%tsp} and @fresh ginger{2%tsp} finely grated. Whisk in enough of the pasta water to make a loose, smooth dressing.

Add the @cucumber{1½%cups} thinly sliced to the bowl on top of the dressing, but don't mix in. Drizzle cucumber lightly with a little more soy sauce.

Add the drained pasta, @scallions{1%bunch} thinly sliced, @crystallized ginger{2%tbsp} chopped and @fresh lime juice{1%tbsp} to the bowl and toss well, adding more pasta water if needed to make a glossy dressing. Taste and add more chile crisp, soy sauce and lime juice as needed. Top with @cilantro or basil{} chopped if you like, then serve.
